            "relpath": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^(?!/)(?!.*\\.\\.)[A-Za-z0-9._/-]{0,512}$"
            },
            "offset": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0
            },
            "length": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0,
              "maximum": 4194304
            },
            "expect_sha256": {
              "$ref": "common.schema.json#/$defs/sha256"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "unevaluatedProperties": false,
      "description": "Round 3 containment (Sol 6 new finding): the executor opens the file by walking from a directory fd of the job's output root, one component at a time with O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY (final component O_NOFOLLOW, then fstat S_ISREG), so no symlink or '..' can leave the root; it reads only from that fd and refuses with conflict 'output changed' if the opened file's size/sha256 differ from expect_sha256 (the value job-output-list returned): a path swapped between list and get is refused. Reference: tests/contracts_v2/validation.py contained_open(). Round 4 (Sol 6 r3) trusted staging: the job unit writes only into a fresh per-job staging directory owned by the job account. After the unit is stopped and its cgroup is empty, the executor (via flightctl-helper output-collect) walks staging with O_NOFOLLOW, accepts only regular files with st_nlink == 1 and st_uid == the job account (checked with fstat on the opened fd), and COPIES their bytes into the job's directory in an executor-owned output store, recording each copy's sha256. Everything else (symlink, hard link, device, fifo, foreign owner) is skipped and listed as rejected. job-output-list/get serve only those copies, so smuggled hard links never reach a reader. Absolute or '..' paths are refused before the walk. Reference: stage_outputs(), contained_open()."
    },
